"268",""
"269",""
"270",""
"271","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) came out to them while they were sitting, and he said: ""Shall I not inform you of the best of people in status?"" We said: ""Yes."" He said: ""A man holding the reins of his horse"" — or he said: ""a horse in the path of Allah until he dies or is killed."" He said: ""Shall I inform you of the one next to him?"" We said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""A man secluded in a mountain pass, establishing prayer and giving zakah, and keeping away from people."" He said: ""Shall I inform you of the worst of people in status?"" We said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""The one who is asked in the name of Allah the Great and does not give."""
