"331","On the authority of Aisha, she said: I went out on the day of the Trench (Khandaq) following the tracks of the people. She said: I heard the vibration of the earth behind me - meaning: the sound of the earth. She said: I turned around and there was Sa'd ibn Mu'adh with his nephew al-Harith ibn Aws carrying his shield. She said: I sat on the ground and Sa'd passed by wearing a coat of mail of iron whose edges protruded, and I feared for Sa'd's extremities. He passed by while reciting: Wait a little, the camel will catch up to the battle. How excellent is death when the appointed time has come. She said: I stood up and entered a garden where there was a group of Muslims, among them Umar ibn al-Khattab, and among them a man wearing a helmet. Umar said: What brought you here? You are indeed bold! She said: He kept blaming me until I wished the earth would split open for me. She said: The man lifted the helmet from his face and it was Talha ibn Ubaydullah. He said: O Umar! Where is the gathering or flight except to Allah? She said: A man from the polytheists of Quraysh called Ibn al-Ariqah shot an arrow at Sa'd and said: Take this, and I am Ibn al-Ariqah. It hit his vein and severed it. Sa'd invoked Allah saying: O Allah, do not let me die until You cool my eyes regarding Banu Qurayza. She said: They were his allies and clients in the pre-Islamic period. His wound healed, and Allah sent the wind upon the polytheists, and Allah sufficed the believers. Abu Sufyan went to Tihama, Uyaynah ibn Badr went to Najd, and Banu Qurayza fortified themselves. The Messenger of Allah returned to Medina and ordered a tent for Sa'd in the mosque. Gabriel came with dust on his teeth and said: Have you laid down the weapons? By Allah, the angels have not yet laid down the weapons. Go out to Banu Qurayza and fight them. The Messenger of Allah put on his armor and besieged them for twenty-five nights. They said: Descend on the judgment of the Messenger of Allah. They consulted Abu Lubabah who gestured slaughter. They said: We descend on the judgment of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh."
"332",""
"333",""
"334",""
"335",""
"336",""
"337","Ibn Abbas narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) visited a man from the Ansar. When he drew near his house, he heard him speaking inside. When he sought permission and entered, he saw no one. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: ""I heard you speaking to someone else?"" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I had gone inside, distressed by people's talk on account of the fever I had, when someone entered upon me. I have never seen a man after you with a more honorable sitting nor better speech than him."" He said: ""That was Gabriel (peace be upon him). And indeed among you are men who, if one of them were to swear by Allah, He would fulfill it."""
"338",""
"339",""
"340",""
"341",""
"342",""
"343",""
"344","On the authority of Sulaymān ibn Ziyād al-Ḥaḍramī, that ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Juzʾ al-Zubaydī narrated to him that he passed by Ayman with a companion of his, and a group of Quraysh had removed their lower garments and made them into strips with which they were striking one another, while they were naked. ʿAbdullāh said: ""When we passed by them, they said, 'These are monks, so leave them alone.'"" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came out to them. When they saw him, they scattered. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) returned angry until he entered [his house], and I was behind the chamber, so I heard him saying: ""Glory be to Allah! They neither felt shame before Allah, nor did they cover themselves before the Messenger of Allah."" And Umm Ayman was with him, saying: ""Ask forgiveness for them, O Messenger of Allah."" ʿAbdullāh said: ""The Prophet said: 'By no means shall I ask forgiveness for them.'"""
"345",""
"346",""
"347",""
"348",""
"349",""
"350",""
"351",""
"352","On the authority of Abū Dharr, who said, marfūʿan: ""Upon every person, on every day the sun rises, there is a charity due from him upon himself."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! From where do I give charity when we possess no wealth?"" He said: ""For indeed among the doors of charity are: the takbīr, the tasbīḥ, the taḥmīd, the tahlīl, the istighfār, enjoining good, forbidding evil, removing the thorn from the path of people, the bone, and the stone, guiding the blind, making the deaf and the mute understand until they comprehend, guiding the seeker to a need he has whose location you know, striving with the strength of your legs to the distressed one crying for help, and supporting the weak with the strength of your arms. All of that is from the doors of charity from you upon yourself. And for you in your sexual intercourse with your wife is a reward."" Abū Dharr said: ""How can there be a reward for me in my desire?"" He said: ""Do you see, if you had a child, then he reached maturity and you hoped for his goodness, then he died, would you seek reward for him?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""So you created him?"" He said: ""Rather, Allah created him."" He said: ""So you guided him?"" He said: ""Rather, Allah guided him."" He said: ""So you provided for him?"" He said: ""Rather, Allah was the One providing for him."" He said: ""Likewise, so place it in its lawful place and avoid its unlawful place; for if Allah wills, He will give it life, and if He wills, He will cause it to die, and for you is a reward."""
